# One mistake, two errors: reading a struct's constructor parameter that is not a field (no pun, so not a member) as a
# member gives "S has no member 'flag'" and then, at the same place, "a condition is a Bool, found I32" - the unknown
# member recovers as an I32 and the condition is checked against it. Found building store.olang's familiarity table
# (a constructor parameter read as s.Familiarity before it was punned). Expected: the first error alone (one error per
# cause). Actual (olang ada716d): both. Fix in the program: pun the parameter (a line "flag" in the body).
type S struct(flag Bool = false) {
    n I64 = 0
}

fn main() ? {
    s := S()
    if s.flag { println("yes") }
}
